You're responding to the mail I sent you some time ago?

What I do when I have only web access is to open an editor window (use
any mono-space(!) text editor that allows the line width to be defined
and wraps the text at that width), write in there and copy/paste it into
the goo*** window.

Another possibility is to use the "preview" button in goo*** instead of
the post-button, so you can inspect what it looks like before posting.
(But that can be quite tedious, if you have written a lot of text, and
you switch back and forth between the edit and the preview window.)

I guess the third possibility might be (haven't tried, though) to write
the lines completely without breaks (ie. write them only at paragraph
boundaries); then goo*** might do the line breaks at position 70.

